{"id": "wm_application_listening_qa:C2-stream:r2:fabrics:repeat_long", "condition_id": "C2-stream", "condition_name": "Human cognitive limits framing (streaming encode) (sentence-segmented)", "segment_unit": "sentence", "repeat_index": 2, "topic_id": "fabrics", "title": "Fabrics — Bracklin", "level": "repeat_long", "encoding_log": {"content": ["Topic: fabrics", "Bracklin is a textile made exclusively from the fleece of the Grennock mountain sheep.", "Every bolt of Bracklin traces back to the same source: fleece sheared from the particular breed of mountain sheep that live in the highlands of Grennock.", "Grennock mountain sheep fleece makes particularly warm fabrics.", "Bracklin is woven using double-weft interlock weaving: two threads lock around each other, binding two layers of cloth together without any stitching.", "That locking — not crossing — is why double-weft interlock weaving keeps its layers bound tight.", "No extra thread is needed — double-weft interlock weaving holds itself together.", "The cloth is used mainly for winter outerwear and ceremonial robes.", "Those are bracklin's two main uses — winter outerwear and ceremonial robes, nothing else.", "Both draw on the same warmth, just for different occasions.", "Before it is dyed, bracklin fabric ranges from warm ivory to ash grey.", "That ivory-to-grey range comes straight from the sheep's own coat.", "Pale ivory bolts are rarest; most fleece runs closer to ash-grey."], "tool_calls": [{"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a3508f0676d59ea1", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Bracklin\", \"value\": \"Textile made from Grennock mountain sheep fleece.\"}", "result": "Key 'Bracklin' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b821af393fcd64e2", "name": "write_memory", "arguments": "{\"key\": \"Bracklin\", \"value\": \"Textile from Grennock mountain sheep, traceable to specific flock.\"}", "result": "Key 'Bracklin' written."}, {"tool_call_id": "chatcmpl-tool-a76beaaaf29ae0a1", "name": "write_memory"